This is what I drew.

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:21.370
That's so cute!

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:22.960
I completed mine too.

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:26.670
Isn't it really well done?

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:29.000
Sorry, I'm not sure what to make of it.

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:30.670
I see...

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:32.720
Then, wait one second!

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:34.510
Tadaa!

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:36.720
Animals of the savannah!

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:39.430
What do you think?

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:41.850
Sorry, I'm having an even harder
time with this one.

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:46.480
My neighbor, Sae, is also an art student.

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:48.650
Like me, she's a second-year.

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:51.070
She's a novelist.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:54.450
Wow, that's amazing.

00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:00.080
Come to think of it, the deadline
for her novel is tomorrow.

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:02.160
She said she's stayed up for four nights.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:03.830
Let's go back to my place.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:05.120
Are we going to leave her like this?

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:08.460
She'll be all right. I'll bring her dinner later.

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:11.590
This place attracts eccentric art students.

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:12.460
Eccentric 3

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:20.850
I'll show you places where you
can shop and do errands.

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:22.890
Thank you very much.

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:25.940
Come to think of it, did you know that
there's a public bath nearby?

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:28.610
I still haven't gone there.

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:32.780
Wow! I've never been to a public bath!

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:34.740
Then, it's decided!

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.990
If I'm not mistaken, it's closed today.

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:39.620
What? Really?

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:41.660
I-I'm lying though.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:43.620
What?! Lying?!

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.540
Why did you lie, Hiro?

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:50.590
I'm sorry, you see...

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:52.210
Let's go to the bath!

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:56.130
Please! I don't want to go today!

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:58.930
How come? Why?

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.640
To tell you the truth...

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:05.020
I was going to save it for tomorrow,
but I couldn't resist.

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:14.650
There's a great cake shop nearby.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:16.150
I see.

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:19.570
There's no one to stop you
when you're on your own.

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:22.280
That's right, that's the problem.

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:27.540
You should have told me.
I would have eaten it for you!

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:31.380
You'd be able to maintain your diet,
and I'd have something to eat.

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:32.670
We'll make an easy profit!

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:35.960
I don't think you're using
that phrase properly.

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:39.090
That aside, even though it's your
first time living on your own,

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:40.590
you're quite brave, aren't you, Miya-chan?

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:42.350
You even moved in early.

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:44.310
March 5
Miyako Moves In

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:48.810
That's amazing, Miya-chan!

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:52.730
I'm still nervous about whether I can do this.

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:55.530
It's nothing special.

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:58.570
I got used to it quickly.
You will too, Yunocchi.

00:18:58.570 --> 00:18:59.950
You think so?

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:03.240
Miya-chan, don't talk with your mouth full.

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:06.200
Anyway, back to what we were talking about...

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:08.750
Miya-chan, why did you decide to come here?

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:12.210
After I finished the exam,
I saw the Hidamari Apartments

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:14.500
and thought that it was great
that it was so close.

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:16.750
I wanted to live here.

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:19.880
You were confident that you'd
be accepted, weren't you?

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:24.300
Yuno, you came by yourself too, right?

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:25.140
Yes.

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:27.350
Since I'll be living here by myself,

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:30.690
I figured that I should do everything
myself from the first day.

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:32.400
Besides, if I didn't do that,

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:35.570
my parents would come along
with me and do everything.

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:38.480
I figured that things wouldn't be any
different from before if that happened.

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:40.490
That's impressive, Yuno!

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:43.700
Huh? No way, it's not that impressive!

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:47.160
I slept all the way here.

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:48.790
On the train?

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.750
No, on the movers' truck.

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:54.460
Being overly nervous is tiring, isn't it?

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:57.920
I don't remember when I fell asleep at all.

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:01.970
When the mover woke me up, we were already
in front of the Hidamari Apartments.

00:20:02.050 --> 00:20:04.260
You must be really something.

00:20:04.260 --> 00:20:05.760
That's not true!

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:07.310
I just fell asleep.

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:09.680
You must have been worn out.

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:10.680
Eccentric?

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:14.350
Oh, look at the time.

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:17.110
I've got to make dinner.

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:20.610
Sorry for staying so long.
I'll be going back to my place!

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:24.570
It's all right. Come again if
you ever need anything.

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:25.990
I will.

00:20:25.990 --> 00:20:28.450
I'll come to you whenever
I have any problems.

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:30.160
O-Okay...

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:33.210
I'm home.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:37.460
Oh, I forgot...

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:42.550
I've got to put this out first.

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:45.510
Look, it's your new home.

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:51.180
I'm worn out.

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:55.400
But I'm glad that everyone is fun to be with.

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:59.320
I get the feeling that I'll have fun here.

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:01.280
Yunocchi!

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:02.530
Miya-chan!

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:04.400
I don't have running water.

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:06.160
Let me in.

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:10.910
I'm a little anxious though.

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:14.910
Sae, are you all right?

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:18.170
I'm sorry about earlier.

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:22.880
The girl who was with me is a new student.

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:24.800
Her name is Yuno.

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:29.430
She just moved in today,
so we should help her out.

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:32.560
Okay, I could tell, since things were noisy.

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:35.180
Is she in room 201? 203?

00:21:35.390 --> 00:21:38.560
201, Misato Sempai's old room.

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:41.400
She's a very small and cute girl.

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:43.820
201, huh?

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:46.780
I hope there aren't any strange
devices left over.

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:48.030
Yeah!

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:51.280
That aside, is it good, Sae?

00:21:51.280 --> 00:21:52.490
Sorry.

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:55.330
Yeah, it's really good.

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:57.960
Hiro - Room 101 - Second Year
Motherly - Good at Cooking

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:00.920
Sae - Room 102 - Second Year
Beautiful and Intelligent
Knowledgeable in Many Subjects

00:22:03.210 --> 00:22:05.130
Miyako - Room 202 - First Year
Artless - Straightforward

00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:08.130
Yuno - Room 201 - First Year
Stable Family - Hard Worker

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:10.140
The End
To Be Continued

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:25.900
An unknown world stretched out

00:22:25.900 --> 00:22:31.620
Connecting, endless connecting threads

00:22:32.280 --> 00:22:38.660
An upside down world is pretty fun

00:22:38.660 --> 00:22:44.460
Connecting, never-ending threads

00:22:44.840 --> 00:22:50.550
You are smiling somewhere today

00:22:51.090 --> 00:22:56.140
I will run all night until the day we meet again

00:22:56.140 --> 00:22:57.730
Run all night

00:22:57.730 --> 00:23:00.810
The record of a resounding shooting star

00:23:00.810 --> 00:23:04.150
Your singing voice

00:23:04.150 --> 00:23:07.190
Touches my heart

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:10.490
A sky full of shooting stars

00:23:10.490 --> 00:23:13.620
The record of a shining shooting star

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:16.830
Your whispering voice

00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:20.250
Leads me through space

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:23.130
A song about shooting stars

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:26.670
I can't hear them

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:30.590
I can't reach them

00:23:30.590 --> 00:23:35.140
The footsteps I'm looking for

00:23:40.020 --> 00:23:41.020
Preview

00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:42.310
Preview
It's almost time.

00:23:42.310 --> 00:23:43.350
Preview
It sure is.

00:23:43.350 --> 00:23:45.520
Preview
Oh yeah, I need to buy some black-eyed peas.

00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:47.360
Preview
I always think it's strange,

00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:49.820
Preview
but black-eyed peas and azuki beans
look exactly alike, don't they?

00:23:49.820 --> 00:23:51.700
Preview
Why can't you use azuki beans?

00:23:51.700 --> 00:23:53.990
Preview
When you boil azuki beans, the skin breaks.

00:23:53.990 --> 00:23:56.490
Preview
People disliked it because it
reminded them of seppuku.

00:23:56.490 --> 00:23:59.000
Preview
Typical Sae! You're a walking encyclopedia.

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:01.410
Preview
But I'm going to be making it.

00:24:01.410 --> 00:24:04.630
Preview
The next episode is
"February 2, Sakura Sakura"

00:24:04.630 --> 00:24:06.090
Preview
We'll be waiting at Hidamari Apartments.

00:24:06.090 --> 00:24:07.800
Preview
Be sure to tune in!

00:24:07.800 --> 00:24:09.380
Preview
